.TH "libnvmf_exclusion_add_ctrl" 9 "libnvmf_exclusion_add_ctrl" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvmf_exclusion_add_ctrl \- append an entry built from a controller.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "int" libnvmf_exclusion_add_ctrl
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ","
.BI "const char *name "  ","
.BI "struct libnvme_ctrl *c "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
libnvme global context; must not be NULL
.IP "name" 12
list name
.IP "c" 12
connected controller; the entry's transport, traddr, trsvcid,
subsysnqn and (when set) host-iface are taken from it
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Builds the exclusion entry from the controller's transport parameters inside
libnvme -- the caller needs no knowledge of the on-disk entry format -- then
appends it via \fBlibnvmf_exclusion_add\fP.  Creates the list if it does not
exist.
.SH "RETURN"
0 on success, -EINVAL if \fIctx\fP or \fIc\fP is NULL or the controller lacks
a transport/traddr/subsysnqn, negative errno otherwise.
